      "query_signature": "Choose $x_t\\in[0,1]^d$ and then observe one noisy value at that point: $$Y_t=f_t(x_t)+Z_t,\\qquad Z_t\\overset{\\mathrm{i.i.d.}}\\sim\\mathcal N(0,\\sigma^2).$$. Noise is independent across rounds and independent of the algorithm; only the current action point is observed. Causal randomized policies are allowed and $d,T,k,B,\\sigma$ is public. The drift budget is hidden, so the same policy cannot depend on $V_{\\mathcal H}$. Received feedback may be stored and reused computationally. No unrevealed historical information or extra queries to exhausted samples are available; any within-round full-function or common-sample access must be explicit.",
